summary:
@RexDouglass Anyway, I stand by this take. Relevant to your dustup today.
Quoting @beenwrekt
Interrupted time series are the lowest form of causal inference.

@Tyler_A_Harper Analogous to the smoking-cancer debates.
The evidence that smoking causes cancer *is* hard to parse and interpret.
But the evidence that smoking a pack of cigarettes makes you feel like shit is unequivocal. We didn't need science to know that smoking was a fucked up behavior.

@AnilMakam @bmj_latest The treatment arm wasn't provided masks. They were provided gift cards to buy masks.
The control group was explicitly told not to wear masks.
All interaction (recruitment, instructions, assessment) was through online portals.

@dandekadt I know you're joking, but from that post:
"Since 1996, the university has added 835 faculty and 11648 administrators."
Faculty being lazy and selfish does not explain this trend.
